    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and high-efficiency matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12). Facing Leahy, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable SP_xERA (4.52) and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his score well into the elite tier. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (74.32) and **Trea Turner** (67.06) are essential foundations; **Christian Yelich** leverages a strong park factor and platoon edge against Kelly, while **Trea Turner** remains our primary engine for stolen bases despite a slight efficiency penalty due to Wacha\u2019s pickoff capabilities. **Caleb Durbin** (66.45) also stands out as a high-upside play, buoyed by a prime opportunity against Aldegheri that justifies his aggressive deployment in the #5 spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Luke Raley** (58.60). While he boasts a strong matchup against Bieber\u2019s high xERA, he was ultimately edged out by **Yordan Alvarez** (58.67), whose elite xwOBA (0.477) provides a higher floor even in a tougher matchup against Rasmussen. We are proceeding with caution regarding the weather, specifically the 40% rain risk hovering over the contest featuring **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.71); while both are projected as strong starts, their fantasy output remains susceptible to disruption. Finally, while **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.90) occupies a slot today, his performance against Gilbert, L will be monitored closely, as the SP skill differential presents our most significant hurdle for a high-scoring offensive output in this lineup.",
